Make Your Mark: BlackLine’s BDR team is already performing well, and we’re looking for a Regional Manager, Business Development to make it better without breaking what works. You’ll lead a hybrid inbound and outbound BDR team that creates pipeline across several European markets, from mid-market to mega-enterprise accounts.
This is a chance to turn outbound from a volume game into a strategic, researched, multi-threaded engine, and to get AEs to act on the pipeline your team sources, even when they’re deep in late-stage deals at quarter-end.
You’ll inherit a team that already performs, with a mix of experienced and newer BDRs. You’ll have direct visibility to senior leaders across Europe, a clear line from your work to commercial results, and a “come and prove it” culture with real progression, including a growing number of sales and leadership openings in London.
You’ll report to the Hiring Manager, based in California, and have the autonomy to set the agenda, launch initiatives and build relationships without waiting for direction. For the first six months, we want you to assess the team and its processes, keep what works, and bring your own perspective on what to improve.
You'll Get To:
What you will own
• The territory map and account allocation for your region;
• Hiring, onboarding and development of the team;
• Coaching and development for your BDRs: call reviews, Gong recordings, role-play, messaging and objection handling, adapted to each person;
• Your team’s rhythm: planning, one-to-ones, performance reviews, call blitzes, and forecast and pipeline calls with sales leaders;
• Relationships with AEs, sales leaders, RevOps and three regional marketing teams, including events, campaigns and post-event follow-up;
• A succession pipeline, so BDRs have a clear route into AE roles or leadership.
How we work
• We qualify with MEDDIC, and BDRs attend every discovery call they book;
• Our tech stack includes Salesforce, LinkedIn, ZoomInfo, Gong, dialers (Orum, Nooks) and cadence tools (Gong Engage, Outreach, Salesloft or similar);
• We expect AI-forward working, from you personally and with your team. Tools support the strategy; they don’t replace it.
What You'll Bring:
• Experience leading a BDR team, and the ability to explain how you run your week, spot high and low performance, and address both;
• Clear communication with everyone, including in difficult conversations with senior stakeholders. You’d rather have the awkward conversation early than let it sit;
• The ability to describe a time something went wrong and how you pulled out of it, and to tell it straight;
• A genuine interest in BDRs’ next career steps, and excitement about their progression more than about your own title;
• Experience building BDRs who think for themselves rather than depend on you;
• A view of success based on which accounts are worked, which stakeholders are reached and how many conversations become opportunities, not on activity numbers alone;
• Hands-on use of AI for your own work and with your team, beyond surface-level use;
• Comfort working in Salesforce.
Thrive at BlackLine Because You Are Joining:
• A technology-based company with a sense of adventure and a vision for the future. Every door at BlackLine is open. Just bring your brains, your problem-solving skills, and be part of a winning team at the world's most trusted name in Finance Automation!
• A culture that is kind, open, and accepting. It's a place where people can embrace what makes them unique, and the mix of cultural backgrounds and varying interests cultivates diverse thought and perspectives.
• A culture where BlackLiner's continued growth and learning is empowered. BlackLine offers a wide variety of professional development seminars and inclusive affinity groups to celebrate and support our diversity.
BlackLine is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to sex, gender identity or expression, race, ethnicity, age, religious creed, national origin, physical or mental disability, ancestry, color, marital status, sexual orientation, military or veteran status, status as a victim of domestic violence, sexual assault or stalking, medical condition, genetic information, or any other protected class or category recognized by applicable equal employment opportunity or other similar laws.
BlackLine recognizes that the ways we work and the workplace itself has shifted. We innovate in a workplace that optimizes a combination of virtual and in-person interactions to maximize collaboration and nurture our culture. Candidates who live within a reasonable commute to one of our offices will work in the office at least 3 days a week.
Accommodations:
BlackLine is committed to creating an inclusive and accessible experience for all candidates. If you require a reasonable accommodation that would better enable your success during the application or interview process, please complete this form.

&nbsp;About CarbonChain&nbsp;
The fight against Climate Change is evolving rapidly. Climate tech is changing. The first wave was reporting. The next is treating carbon the way companies treat money: as a way to decide what to buy, who to sell to, and which incentives to claim.&nbsp;
Around the world, carbon is becoming a condition of trade. Border taxes, free allocations, green premiums, cheaper capital. It looks a lot like the post-war rebuild: governments put capital and tax incentives on the table, and the companies that could keep the books moved first. The missing piece then was bookkeeping. The missing piece now is the same, carbon accounting.&nbsp;
CarbonChain is that bookkeeping. We turn messy, real-world supply-chain data into numbers a trader, a sustainability lead, or a CFO will actually use.&nbsp;
We want people who are agents of change, who feel the impact of climate change and know there is no way around it to create a better future for every being.&nbsp; &nbsp;
People who know the customer is the truth of how a company thrives. People who treat data as the fuel for how fast society can change. People who use AI to accelerate the cause for good by working through an AI lens first to automate repetitive tasks and analyse data. Finally, people who enjoy working with people.&nbsp;
Our Product&nbsp;
We help the world's largest commodity producers and traders measure and cut emissions, with verified primary data where we can get it and defensible defaults where we cannot. The platform turns operational and supplier files into decision-grade carbon and compliance insight: sourcing, CBAM, product and corporate footprints, reporting customers and regulators will stand behind.&nbsp;
We organise carbon accounting around the user in four contexts at once:&nbsp;
• Immediate: the tools in front of them&nbsp;
• Internal: how they work with colleagues&nbsp;
• External: how they work with suppliers and customers&nbsp;
• Societal: how they work with society, governments, and disclosing bodies&nbsp;
The data we hold is only useful if it makes all four of those jobs easier.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Head of Engineering&nbsp;
About the Role&nbsp;
We’re looking for a Head of Engineering to lead our engineering team through its next stage of growth. Reporting to CEO, you’ll own how we build: our technical direction, architecture, quality standards, delivery process, and, most importantly, the team itself.&nbsp;
This is a leadership role rather than a hands-on coding one. Your impact will come through the decisions you steer, the standards you set, and the engineers you hire and grow. You’ll still need deep technical credibility to challenge designs, weigh trade-offs, and earn the trust of engineers and customers alike.&nbsp;
As a startup, we move fast and make pragmatic decisions. You’ll balance speed with quality in a domain where data accuracy, auditability, and trust are non-negotiable. You’ll also act as the voice of technology across the business and with our customers, and help shape how CarbonChain uses AI, both in engineering and across the company.&nbsp;
What You’ll Do&nbsp;
• Own technical strategy and decision-making: set the direction for our platform, make and document key technical decisions, and keep engineering aligned with company goals as they evolve&nbsp;
• Steer architectural decisions across our system, from ingestion pipelines and provenance tracking to CBAM data sharing workflows, so that what we build is scalable, reliable, and audit-ready&nbsp;
• Build, coach, and nurture the team through hiring, onboarding, regular 1:1s, career development, and performance management, creating an environment where engineers do their best work and want to stay&nbsp;
• Own quality across engineering by defining our QA strategy, testing approach, and code review practices. You won’t review every PR, but you’ll make sure reviews are consistent, effective, and uphold our standards&nbsp;
• Build and maintain an engineering process playbook covering how we plan, scope, ship, handle incidents, and learn from retrospectives, and mature it as the team grows without adding unnecessary bureaucracy&nbsp;
• Make sure priorities are well maintained and balanced by working with Product, Sales, Customer Success, and the Carbon Team to agree trade-offs between new features, technical debt, reliability, and customer commitments&nbsp;
• Lead AI adoption in the engineering team, through AI-assisted development, tooling, and workflows, and across the wider business, identifying high-value opportunities and setting sensible guardrails given the sensitivity of customer data&nbsp;
• Act as the face of technology at CarbonChain: join client calls where needed, explain our architecture and data handling to enterprise customers, and support security and procurement conversations&nbsp;
• Partner with the leadership team on headcount planning, engineering budget, tooling, and infrastructure costs&nbsp;
• Champion a culture of ownership, pragmatism, and customer focus, staying comfortable with ambiguity and changing priorities while keeping the long-term picture in mind&nbsp;
What We’re Looking For&nbsp;
• Extensive experience in software engineering, including significant exposure leading engineering teams, ideally at a scaling startup or SaaS company&nbsp;
• A strong technical foundation in modern web applications and distributed systems, with enough fluency in Python, TypeScript, cloud architecture, IaC/Terraform, and CI/CD to steer decisions confidently without writing production code yourself&nbsp;
• A proven track record of hiring, coaching, and retaining engineers, and of building healthy, high-performing team cultures&nbsp;
• Experience introducing and maturing engineering processes such as delivery planning, QA, code review, and incident management in a growing team&nbsp;
• Sound, pragmatic judgement on trade-offs between speed, quality, and long-term maintainability&nbsp;
• Strong collaboration skills: you work closely with the Founders, Product and Commercial teams to shape priorities, advise on feasibility, and make decisions together&nbsp;
• Excellent communication skills, including explaining complex technical topics to non-technical colleagues and being credible and confident in front of enterprise customers&nbsp;
• Hands-on experience driving AI adoption in engineering teams, and curiosity about how AI can improve the wider business&nbsp;
&nbsp;
• Bonus: experience with data-intensive systems, particularly where data quality, lineage, or auditability matter&nbsp;
• Bonus: understanding of security and compliance frameworks such as SOC 2 or ISO 27001&nbsp;
• Bonus: experience in climate tech or sustainability&nbsp;
&nbsp;
How We Work&nbsp;
As a hybrid co-located team, we're inspired by our values and anchored in hubs across the UK and US. This role would be located 3d/week in our London LABS Camden office space.&nbsp;You will need the right to work in the UK.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
What we offer&nbsp;
Meaningful impact and accelerated growth&nbsp;
This is a rare opportunity to work on technology that directly addresses the climate crisis while shaping the future of a fast-growing company. You'll take the lead on engineering strategy, roadmap and team evolution.&nbsp;&nbsp;
You'll tackle diverse challenges, work across the full stack of problems (technical and otherwise), and own meaningful projects from start to finish. If you want to learn quickly, take on real responsibility, and see the direct results of your work, this is the place to do it.&nbsp;
Competitive salary and benefits:&nbsp;
• 28 days annual leave&nbsp;
• £500 home office setup allowance&nbsp;
• £1,000 annual learning allowance&nbsp;
• Private healthcare&nbsp;
• Company pension incl. salary sacrifice options&nbsp;
• Generous parental leave policy&nbsp;
• Weekly team lunches in the office&nbsp;
• Office gym, and cycle to work scheme&nbsp;
• Remote work contribution of £1,000 towards expenses for working abroad&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Equal Opportunity Employer&nbsp;
CarbonChain is dedicated to creating an equitable, inclusive, and supportive work environment that brings people together from diverse backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives. Our strength is in our differences. We're proud to be an equal opportunity employer and are proud to welcome all applicants as we're committed to promoting a culture of opportunity for all.&nbsp;
If you think your skills and experience match what we're looking for and you'd like to join next Climate Tech adventure, please get in touch.&nbsp;
You can find out more about interviewing at CarbonChain at carbonchain.com/careers/interview-process.&nbsp;
CarbonChain values diversity and inclusion and welcomes applications from candidates with diverse backgrounds.&nbsp;
If you think your skills and experience match what we’re looking for and you’d like to join the next Climate Tech industry unicorn, please get in touch!
You can find out more about interviewing at CarbonChain at&nbsp;https://www.carbonchain.com/careers/interview-process.

