Cato Networks is the converged network and security cloud for the AI era.&nbsp;
As AI reshapes cybersecurity, enterprises face a dual challenge: unlocking AI’s potential while defending against AI-driven attacks. Cato addresses both through a unified, cloud-native platform, providing the visibility and context to prioritize risks and stop threats in real time across users, applications, data, and AI agents.&nbsp;
Join us as we scale: take on ambitious technological challenges and shape the next generation of enterprise security at a company trusted by thousands of organizations worldwide.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
We are looking for a Solutions Enablement Manager to help our sales and channel team understand and confidently position Cato’s products and solutions. Reporting to the Director, Sales Enablement, you will be part of the Sales Enablement team and partner closely with Product and Product Marketing to turn product knowledge into practical training and content for our Commercial Account Executives, Sales Directors, and our Channel team members.&nbsp;
You will serve as the Sales Enablement team’s subject matter expert on our solutions, staying current on the product roadmap and helping sellers understand what is changing, why it matters to customers, and how it fits into our broader offering. You will support new product launches, ongoing enhancements, and product refreshers, while working with regional Sales Enablement Leads to deliver relevant training across regions. You should be comfortable learning how our solutions work and helping sellers understand what they do, where they fit, and why they matter to customers. The focus is on helping sellers position our solutions, rather than technical implementation&nbsp;
What you'll will do...
• Partner with Product and Product Marketing to stay current on the roadmap and determine what sellers need to know, how new capabilities fit into existing offerings, and when enablement is needed
• Develop and&nbsp;maintain training and content for product launches, enhancements, and refreshers for sales and Channel teams, ensuring technical accuracy and alignment with Product Marketing messaging
• Keep product learning current across onboarding and ongoing enablement, updating or retiring materials as our solutions evolve
• Serve as the Sales Enablement team’s go-to resource for product and solution knowledge, helping regional Enablement Leads prepare for training and answer seller questions
• Work with regional Sales Enablement Leads to deliver training, adapt materials to regional needs, and equip them to&nbsp;facilitate sessions
• Use seller feedback, knowledge checks, and content engagement data to&nbsp;identify gaps and improve training. Share recurring questions and field insights with Product and Product Marketing&nbsp;
What you'll need..
• 5+ years of relevant experience in Sales Enablement, product enablement or a related role, with experience developing product and solution training focused for sales audiences
• Proven ability to&nbsp;translate technical concepts into clear explanations of customer challenges, business value, and practical sales conversations. Help sellers understand relevant use cases, ask effective discovery questions, and address common objections
• Experience partnering with Product and Product Marketing to support launches and keep training aligned with product changes and approved messaging
• Strong content development and presentation skills, with experience&nbsp;facilitating engaging training for sales teams and equipping others to deliver it
• Ability to build relationships across teams globally, manage multiple enablement priorities, and deliver content and training against changing release timelines
• Experience using learner feedback and training data to&nbsp;identify knowledge gaps and improve learning effectiveness.&nbsp;
Bonus Qualifications...&nbsp;
• Familiarity with the security or IT networking space.&nbsp;

About Us
Engelhart was founded in 2013 by BTG Pactual Group as a commodities trading company. Our business model is “asset light” and highly diversified – giving us the ability to adapt effectively and nimbly to changing market conditions. We have assembled successful multidisciplinary teams, leveraging advanced fundamental analysis with deep quantitative and weather research capabilities.&nbsp; Our activities are underpinned by strong risk management practices and by powerful technology and operational excellence. We have exceptional teams with diverse global backgrounds and decades of experience, and are driven by a highly collaborative culture, across products and competencies.
In 2024, Engelhart acquired Trailstone, a global energy trading and technology company. The acquisition provides us with new expertise, analytics and proprietary technology which is being used to provide risk management and optimisation services to help maximise the value of our clients’ renewable power. The acquisition also expanded Engelhart’s capabilities into physical natural gas across North America, a critical fuel to support the energy transition.
Our talented and experienced individuals work together according to its four company values: Performance, Agility, Collaboration, Entrepreneurship.
About the Role&nbsp;
As a Data Engineer within Engelhart's Finance department, you will build and operate reliable data pipelines connecting the data warehouse and CTRM platform with brokers and Futures Commission Merchants (FCMs), margin and collateral processes, and the wider Finance technology stack. You will help automate manual Finance workflows into tested, monitored jobs, with robust reconciliations and controls that give stakeholders confidence in the completeness and accuracy of financial data.&nbsp;
This will be a full-time role based in our London office and owning the following responsibilities:&nbsp;
• Build, operate and maintain data pipelines between the data warehouse, CTRM platform, brokers and FCMs, margin and collateral processes, and Finance systems.&nbsp;
• Integrate data from the Finance stack, including P&amp;L and F+, SAP General Ledger, Accounts Payable and Accounts Receivable, and bank statements.&nbsp;
• Automate manual Finance processes by developing reliable, tested and monitored jobs that can be operated and supported effectively.&nbsp;
• Implement reconciliations and data controls to identify missing or incomplete records, duplicates and breaks, and produce clear exception and break reporting.&nbsp;
• Ingest and process external files and feeds, including data received over SFTP and in formats such as CSV and XML.&nbsp;
• Investigate data and reconciliation issues, trace discrepancies through source systems and pipelines, and explain P&amp;L or cash breaks to relevant Finance stakeholders.&nbsp;
• Develop and maintain serverless ETL solutions on AWS, using infrastructure as code and CI/CD practices to support consistent, controlled releases.&nbsp;
• Apply strong SQL and Python-based data processing to transform, validate and reconcile data accurately and efficiently.&nbsp;
• Work with Finance and technology stakeholders to understand requirements, improve existing workflows and deliver maintainable solutions with appropriate controls.&nbsp;
• Contribute to improving the reliability, observability and quality of Finance data flows as the business and its systems evolve.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
About You&nbsp;
You will be a practical, analytical data engineer who combines strong software engineering skills with an understanding of Finance processes and controls. You can work with varied data sources, investigate discrepancies and explain the cause of a P&amp;L or cash break clearly. You take ownership of the reliability of the jobs you build and look for opportunities to simplify and automate manual processes.&nbsp;
As a result, we believe the following experiences and skills are essential for application:&nbsp;
• Strong Python development skills, including experience with Pandas and/or Polars, NumPy, and automated testing with pytest.&nbsp;
• Hands-on experience building AWS serverless ETL pipelines, using services such as Lambda, EventBridge, ECS/Fargate, DynamoDB, CloudWatch and S3.&nbsp;
• Experience with AWS Cloud Development Kit (CDK), infrastructure as code and CI/CD pipelines.&nbsp;
• Experience building APIs using Python frameworks, preferably FastAPI.&nbsp;
• Strong SQL skills, including the ability to query, transform, validate and reconcile data.&nbsp;
• Experience ingesting external files and data feeds, including SFTP transfers and formats such as CSV and XML.&nbsp;
• Good understanding of Finance processes and data, with the analytical skills to investigate and clearly explain a P&amp;L or cash break.&nbsp;
• A disciplined approach to testing, monitoring, reconciliation and control design, including checks for completeness, duplicates and exceptions.&nbsp;
• Strong problem-solving skills and attention to detail, with the ability to trace issues across systems and data pipelines.&nbsp;
• Clear communication skills and the ability to work effectively with Finance and technical stakeholders.&nbsp;
The following experience is not required, but highly desirable for this role:&nbsp;
• Experience using Kafka from Python.&nbsp;
• Experience integrating with SAP or treasury systems.&nbsp;
• Exposure to trading data, including positions and P&amp;L.&nbsp;
• Familiarity with dbt and/or Airflow.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
What we offer&nbsp;
• Competitive compensation and participation in Engelhart’s discretionary bonus plan. &nbsp;
• 25 days of annual holiday entitlement, excluding UK public holidays.&nbsp;
• Robust benefits package such as medical, dental, life insurance, generous pension contribution, and supplemental benefits partially subsidised by the Company.  &nbsp;
• Eligibility to receive external and internal training in accordance with our Training &amp; Development Policy.&nbsp;
We believe in inclusivity and are therefore dedicated to ensuring all employees – across gender identity, race, ethnicity, sexual orientation, religion, life experience, background and more – feel welcome and included in the company. We promote diversity because we believe it is essential to our ability to think holistically.
&nbsp;

About Us
Engelhart was founded in 2013 by BTG Pactual Group as a commodities trading company. Our business model is “asset light” and highly diversified – giving us the ability to adapt effectively and nimbly to changing market conditions. We have assembled successful multidisciplinary teams, leveraging advanced fundamental analysis with deep quantitative and weather research capabilities.&nbsp; Our activities are underpinned by strong risk management practices and by powerful technology and operational excellence. We have exceptional teams with diverse global backgrounds and decades of experience, and are driven by a highly collaborative culture, across products and competencies.
In 2024, Engelhart acquired Trailstone, a global energy trading and technology company. The acquisition provides us with new expertise, analytics and proprietary technology which is being used to provide risk management and optimisation services to help maximise the value of our clients’ renewable power. The acquisition also expanded Engelhart’s capabilities into physical natural gas across North America, a critical fuel to support the energy transition.
Our talented and experienced individuals work together according to its four company values: Performance, Agility, Collaboration, Entrepreneurship.
About the Role&nbsp;
As Principal Data Engineer, you will own the intraday and end-of-day data serving layer between the CTRM platform and its downstream consumers. You will shape the architecture, standards and engineering practices that enable teams across the business to access trusted, timely and well-defined data. This is a hands-on technical leadership role with the opportunity to influence how the business builds and uses its data platform.&nbsp;
This will be a full-time role, based in our London office, owning the following&nbsp;responsibilities:&nbsp;
• Own the intraday and EOD data serving layer between the CTRM platform and its consumers, including Market Risk, Credit Risk, Treasury, Finance, Reporting and desk tools.&nbsp;
• Design and maintain robust data schemas and serving contracts, including SQL, APIs and Kafka-based distribution.&nbsp;
• Define data versioning and reproducibility patterns, including as-of timestamps and run IDs, snapshots and incremental updates, with appropriate treatment of position and P&amp;L data.&nbsp;
• Own the CTRM-to-warehouse data pipeline, ensuring reliable ingestion, transformation, validation and delivery to downstream consumers.&nbsp;
• Lead the implementation and production use of the data warehouse serving layer, closing out the current proof of concept and turning it into a production-ready platform.&nbsp;
• Set engineering standards for data modelling, schema evolution, data quality, observability, testing and operational support.&nbsp;
• Build and operate solutions using relevant platform technologies, including ClickHouse, S3, Kafka and schema registry tooling.&nbsp;
• Work closely with stakeholder teams to understand their needs, propose solutions, explain trade-offs and establish clear, dependable data contracts.&nbsp;
• Provide technical leadership to the data engineering team, raising the quality of design and implementation while encouraging collaboration, constructive challenge and continuous improvement.&nbsp;
• Help shape the longer-term data architecture and engineering approach as the business and its data requirements evolve.
&nbsp;
About You&nbsp;
You will be a technically strong and proactive data engineering leader who can turn complex business requirements into robust, scalable data products. You are comfortable supporting multiple teams, bringing forward clear recommendations and new ideas, and engaging constructively when your designs are challenged. You want to help shape the future data architecture of the business, not simply deliver against a predefined specification.&nbsp;
As a result, we believe the following experiences and skills are essential for this role:&nbsp;
• Demonstrable experience designing and building data warehouses; this is a non-negotiable requirement.&nbsp;
• Hands-on production experience with ClickHouse; this is a non-negotiable requirement.&nbsp;
• Experience delivering a columnar OLAP data platform in production, with a strong understanding of analytical query performance and data modelling.&nbsp;
• Practical experience with Kafka and event-driven or streaming data architectures.&nbsp;
• Strong Python engineering skills and sufficient C# literacy to work effectively with systems and codebases that use C#.&nbsp;
• Experience modelling versioned position and P&amp;L data, including point-in-time or as-of views and reproducible runs.&nbsp;
• Experience working in a trading or other time-sensitive, data-intensive business environment.&nbsp;
• Previous technical leadership, including setting standards and guiding engineering decisions.&nbsp;
• Strong stakeholder management and communication skills, with the confidence to put forward solutions, bring ideas into discussions and engage positively with challenge.&nbsp;
• A solution-oriented mindset and the ability to balance the needs of multiple downstream teams while maintaining coherent platform standards.&nbsp;
The following experience is not required, but highly desirable for this role:&nbsp;
• Experience in commodities trading or energy markets.&nbsp;
• Exposure to a Commodity Trading and Risk Management (CTRM) system, such as Orchestrade or Endur.&nbsp;
• Familiarity with dbt and/or data quality frameworks.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
What we offer&nbsp;
• Competitive compensation and participation in Engelhart’s discretionary bonus plan. &nbsp;
• 25 days of annual holiday entitlement, excluding UK public holidays.&nbsp;
• Robust benefits package such as medical, dental, life insurance, generous pension contribution, and supplemental benefits partially subsidised by the Company.  &nbsp;
• Eligibility to receive external and internal training in accordance with our Training &amp; Development Policy.&nbsp;
We believe in inclusivity and are therefore dedicated to ensuring all employees – across gender identity, race, ethnicity, sexual orientation, religion, life experience, background and more – feel welcome and included in the company. We promote diversity because we believe it is essential to our ability to think holistically.
&nbsp;

**Purpose of Job**
The Officer is responsible for providing secretarial and administrative support in OGC.
**Accountabilities & Responsibilities**
- Producing and completing legal documentation and forms (such as execution versions of contracts, signing announcements and confirmations, corporate authorisations, including certificates, shareholder proxies and powers of attorney, and first drafts of standard agreements (e.g. indemnity agreements)
- Filing and archiving of legal documentation in various hard copy and electronic systems using Livelink and the TCRS systems;
- Liaising with internal and external clients on legal matters such as legal due diligence and execution modalities;
- Processing consultancy engagements in accordance with all relevant procedures and approval processes, preparing engagement/consultancy contracts and arranging invoicing;
- Updating legal knowledge management databases held by LTT in Livelink to ensure correct templates and data is used for management reports;
- Managing correspondence as required;
- Assisting with internal reporting for OGC and DCF management in respect to LTT technical cooperation projects;
- Arranging travel, itineraries, visas and process travel expenses in compliance with Bank’s policies and procedures;
- Provide support during absences of other LTT OTE staff;
- Arranging internal events, webinars, meetings and conference calls and receiving visitors;
- Assisting with the arrangement of external events: online and offline;
- Preparing and organising documents for management committee meetings and Board meetings;
- Preparing and amending power point presentations (external and internal and ensuring appropriate EBRD templates are used);
- Performing any other administrative tasks as assigned.
- Producing and completing legal documentation and forms (such as execution versions of contracts, signing announcements and confirmations, corporate authorisations, including certificates, shareholder proxies and powers of attorney, and first drafts of standard agreements (e.g. indemnity agreements).
**Knowledge, Skills, Experience & Qualifications**
**Academic Qualifications**
- Secondary/High School Education.
- A recognised legal secretarial qualification such as the Legal Secretaries Diploma provided by the Institute of Legal Secretaries and PAs is useful but is not essential.
- Fluent English, with excellent written and oral communication skills.
- Knowledge of another language (_e.g._ Russian, German, French, Turkish or Arabic) both written and spoken would be useful (but such knowledge of relevant language is essential for RO-based roles).
**Experience/Knowledge**
- Significant secretarial and administrative experience;
- Experience in organizing legal conferences, events and webinars;
- Experience in administration of technical cooperation projects and coordination of technical consultants would be useful;
- Good organisational skills, proactive and flexible attitude to work essential;
- Ability to use initiative to undertake tasks and projects without guidance;
- Excellent communications skills, including pleasant and efficient telephone manner;
- Attention to detail and eye for accuracy;
- Ability to cope well under pressure;
- Ability to build effective working relationships with clients and colleagues in a multicultural environment;
- Conscientious, reliable and flexible with a professional and helpful attitude;
- Strong team player, with the ability to work efficiently and to handle simultaneous assignments involving a wide range of bank-wide contacts;
- Ability to multi-task while remaining calm and professional and a capacity for hard work;
- Excellent interpersonal manner, including tact and diplomacy;
- Ability to exercise judgment on and deal discretely with confidential/sensitive information and data;
- Confidence to put self forward for various projects and responsibilities and quickly understand what is required of the task in hand.
**Technical Skills**
- Professional user of Microsoft Office 365(Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook,Access, One Drive and Teams).
- Knowledge of EBRD applications: Smart by GEP, TCRS, SAP Funds ECC and Livelink  would be an advantage.
**What is it like to work at the EBRD? / About EBRD** 
Our agile and innovative approach is what makes life at the EBRD a unique experience! You will be part of a pioneering and diverse international organisation, and use your talents to make a real difference to people's lives and help shape the future of the regions we invest in.  
At EBRD, our Values – Inclusiveness, Innovation, Trust, and Responsibility – are at the heart of how we work. We bring these to life through our Workplace Behaviours: listening well and speaking up, collaborating smartly, acting decisively with full commitment, and simplifying to amplify our impact. These principles shape our culture and define our success. We seek individuals who not only share these values but are also committed to embedding them in their daily work, fostering a positive and high-performing environment. 
The EBRD environment provides you with: 
- Varied, stimulating and engaging work that gives you an opportunity to interact with a wide range of experts in the financial, political, public and private sectors across the regions we invest in. 
- A working culture that embraces inclusion and celebrates diversity. Our workforce reflects a broad range of backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences, bringing fresh ideas, energy, and innovation and enhancing our ability to serve our clients, shareholders, and counterparties effectively.
- A hybrid workplace that offers flexibility to teams and individuals; that is based on trust, flexibility and connectedness. 
- An environment that places sustainability, equality and digital transformation at the heart of what we do. 
- A workplace that prioritises employee wellbeing and provides a comprehensive suite of competitive benefits. 
Diversity is one of the Bank’s core values which are at the heart of everything it does.  As such, the EBRD seeks to ensure that everyone is treated with respect and given equal opportunities and works in an inclusive environment. The EBRD encourages all qualified candidates who are nationals of the EBRD member countries to apply regardless of their racial, ethnic, religious and cultural background, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, age, socio-economic background or disability.   
Please note, that due to the high volume of applications received, we regret to inform you that we are unable to provide detailed feedback to candidates who have not been shortlisted (for further consideration).

