Talent Acquisition Support Coordinator (Fixed Term Contract) The Talent Acquisition Support (TAS) coordinator serves as a key member of the Human Resources team, working with the lateral recruitment and early careers teams supporting our operations in EMEA and APAC. This team member will work closely with the HR team in the London office and report into the TAS team in the US.
The role is a Fixed Term, 12 month contract and will be based in our London office, providing support for colleagues across various countries including London, Frankfurt, Madrid, Paris, Stockholm, Singapore, Hong Kong and Australia.
Hours: 09.00 – 17.30, with a 1-hour unpaid lunch break.
Hybrid working: 4 days in the office / 1 day remote work – flexibility may be required to meet business demands.
Key responsibilities and tasks may include:
• Scheduling interviews for EMEA lateral hires.
• Liaising with colleagues to receive completed feedback forms from each interview.
• Maintaining recruitment files and CV logs in line with local data requirements.
• Drafting campus and full-time offer letters for successful candidates in EMEA and APAC and liaising with internal stakeholders for review and distribution.
• Conducting background checks for new hires, working with HR and Compliance.
• Supporting the European campus hiring processes:• Arranging travel and logistics for interviews and assessment centres (in-person and virtual);
• Coordinating campus events across Europe to ensure attendance from key personnel, booking travel and logistics, and liaising with campus and external vendors;
• Processing all invoices for campus expenses and candidate travel; and
• Scheduling the intern training programmes including logistics for pre-Internship Induction days.
• Supporting the UK & EUR Analyst training programme:• Organizing logistics including travel, hotels, sessions, booking exams, etc;
• Processing all invoices for campus expenses and candidate travel; and
• Working with the “GAMP” coordinators to allocate mentors to new hires, connecting mentors/mentees ahead of joining, providing support and setting expectations for mentor involvement
• Working with branding teams, recruiters, and external vendors for recruitment materials and collateral for events and vendor microsites:• Utilizing vendor platforms to input data, and review to understand candidate origination and success of initiatives.
• Supporting ad hoc projects and initiatives such as “Women in Finance” events, and The Sutton Trust initiative.
• Conducting RTW checks for applicants.
• Collate information for onboarding recruiting firms in Mizuho global systems
Qualifications and Experience:
• College degree
• Minimum 2-years experience in a similar recruitment role;
• Strong interpersonal skills - personable, approachable and successful at building relationships;
• The ability to perform well under pressure and adjust priorities as workload dictates;
• A keen eye for detail, proven organisational and administrative skills and logical reasoning;
• Excellent verbal and written communication skills and an ability to work with a variety of stakeholders;
• Ability to represent the firm and HR internally and externally in a polished and professional manner;
• Open and receptive to suggestions and feedback;
• Calm under pressure, flexible and demonstrates a positive attitude;
• Ability to collaborate virtually across various time-zones;
• An interest in lateral and campus recruitment, and in supporting team members in a professional manner, the ideal candidate will be looking to grow.
Greenhill & Co., Inc., part of Mizuho Americas, is focused on providing financial advice on significant mergers, acquisitions, restructurings, financings and capital raising to corporations, partnerships, institutions and governments globally. It acts on behalf of clients throughout the world from its offices in the Americas, EMEA, and APAC.

We are looking to strengthen our Delivery team with a Senior Project Engineer or Senior Contracts Engineer based at Hampton. You will report directly to the Project Manager and your role will be to manage the design (including challenging solutions and identifying opportunities for innovation), construction, commissioning and putting to work of contracts to ensure they are completed in the most efficient manner to the specification, within the time required and within the tender estimate without risk to the health and safety of all concerned while ensuring good customer satisfaction
Key responsibilities will include:
• Input to, manage and update construction programmes ensuring key milestones are met;
• Arrange, chair and participate in collaborative planning sessions to ensure critical activities are programmed with all key stakeholders ;
• Prepare and issue invitations to tender, collate responses and prepare cost benefit analysis with recommendations for award;
• Prepare and circulate requisitions to buyers;
• Technical co-ordination between MWH engineering and supply chain partners;
• Day to day management of site management team ensuring any issues are resolved or escalated;
• Review of consolidated invoices, identifying errors and omissions prior to payment approval;
• Challenge all stakeholders to identify opportunities for innovation, doing something differently and improving working practises to realise opportunities and minimise risk – both to safety and commercial performance;
• Management and coordination of the risk register and provide monthly updates. Assist Project Managers to manage early warnings to variations to risk register with the project management team; • Attend Health & Safety, Progress, Employee Forums and Coordination meetings as required;
• Work with the Project Manager, Health & Safety, Design and Construction teams to report on all near misses / unsafe conditions/ accidents/ incidents;
• Preparation of pre-start packs and collation and uploading of collated data to systems
• Work closely with Project Quantity Surveyor to generate cost plans, input commitments and monitor project out-turn costs, reporting to the PM any variations and assist in preparation of mitigation plans
• Champion design liaison meetings
• Ensure that all Health and Safety procedures are adhered to and that all activities are carried out with due regard to the Health and Safety of all employees, Clients and members of the general public;

Established in 2004, OLIVER is the world’s first and only specialist in designing, building, and running bespoke in-house agencies and marketing ecosystems for brands. We partner with over 300 clients in 40+ countries and counting. Our unique model drives creativity and efficiency, allowing us to deliver tailored solutions that resonate deeply with audiences.&nbsp;
As a part of The Brandtech Group, we're at the forefront of leveraging cutting-edge AI technology to revolutionise how we create and deliver work. Our AI solutions enhance efficiency, spark creativity, and drive insightful decision-making, empowering our teams to produce innovative and impactful results.&nbsp;
Role: Account Director (6 Month FTC)
Location: London/ Slough, United Kingdom&nbsp; (2-3 days a week from our Client's Slough Offices)
About the role:&nbsp;
&nbsp;
As Account Director, working within our client, &amp; global FMCG business; you are the trusted day-to-day partner for client and the person who keeps complex, multi-platform projects on track. You'll work closely with strategy, creative, production and account colleagues to turn briefs into effective campaigns, with a strong focus on social media and digital content. You'll be accountable for delivery, client satisfaction and project profitability across several projects at once.
What you will be doing:&nbsp;
• Build a collaborative, trusted relationship with client stakeholders, acting as their first point of contact and protecting the brand across every project.
• Stay close to the client to understand their needs, anticipate issues and resolve them early.
• Be accountable for integrated creative projects from brief to fulfilment, maintaining client satisfaction throughout.
• Work with strategy and account colleagues to shape social strategy and milestones for the client.
• Agree campaign scope with the client, then produce estimates and timing plans in our internal scheduling system, including for complex, cross-platform social projects.
• Schedule projects against the right internal resource and help source external resource where needed.
• Partner with digital, video, photography and print producers to bring the right skills together for integrated campaigns.
• Keep projects on process, on time and on budget, motivating and coordinating teams through tight deadlines.
• Be responsible for the financial health of your projects, including profitability, forecasting accuracy and fee discussions. Make sure everyone understands the cost impact of delays, extra amends and re-briefs.
• Report on project income accurately and on time, and escalate invoicing or estimate queries to senior account and business leadership.
• Evaluate project results, both qualitative and quantitative, against the original objectives.
• Guide internal stakeholders through production processes, and spot and act on ad hoc opportunities as they arise.
&nbsp;
What you need to be great in this role:&nbsp;
• Experience managing digital and integrated campaigns in a creative or production agency, with a strong record of delivering across multiple platforms, particularly social media.
• Ideally FMCG experience
• Proficient to expert capability in Account Management and Project Management, with confidence running several complex projects at once.
• Experience working alongside video and photography producers as part of a joined-up approach to campaign delivery.
• Experience with project scheduling and sourcing resource and production services.
• Strong client engagement skills, with the ability to organise, influence and build effective working relationships.
• Clear, courteous communication across strategy, creative, production and client teams.
• Close attention to detail, sound commercial awareness and a sharp eye for project risk.
• Comfort integrating with a client-side team while maintaining a top-tier agency service.
• Nice to have: experience creating content for CMS and e-commerce platforms.
• Advanced use of Gen AI tools relevant to account management to improve output quality and efficiency
• Experience designing AI-assisted workflows for yourself and your team
• Agentic thinking for complex, multi-step challenges
• Strong understanding of AI capabilities and limitations, with rigorous human oversight
