The quality of renewable energy infrastructure depends on every stage of construction, from initial installation through to final inspection and handover. Delivering projects to the required technical standards takes consistent quality control, sound engineering judgement and close coordination on site.
At SUNOTEC, we deliver large-scale renewable energy infrastructure across Europe, with more than 680 projects completed and over 15 GW of installed capacity. Our expertise covers solar PV, battery energy storage, grid infrastructure and lifecycle services.
As our project portfolio in the UK continues to grow, we're looking for a Site QA/QC Engineer to support the quality and successful delivery of our renewable energy construction projects.
Why this role matters:
Quality assurance is essential to delivering renewable energy projects that meet technical specifications, contractual requirements and client expectations.
As a Site QA/QC Engineer, you'll take responsibility for implementing and monitoring quality standards throughout construction. From reviewing technical documentation and carrying out site inspections to identifying non-conformances and ensuring corrective actions are completed, your work will directly influence installation quality and project delivery.
Working closely with project managers, site teams and subcontractors, you'll help prevent defects, maintain compliance with applicable UK regulations and ensure completed works meet the requirements for inspection and handover.
Where you'll make an impact:
- Take ownership of implementing project quality requirements, ensuring the Quality Management System (QMS) is consistently applied across EPC construction activities;
- Ensure construction works comply with approved drawings, technical specifications, contractual requirements, applicable British Standards and UK construction regulations;
- Oversee site inspections and testing activities, ensuring all works are checked against approved Inspection and Test Plans (ITPs) and project quality requirements;
- Identify, document and manage non-conformances, working with site teams and subcontractors to implement corrective and preventive actions and minimize rework;
- Maintain accurate quality records, inspection reports, audit findings and supporting documentation required throughout construction and final handover;
- Work closely with project managers, site managers and subcontractors to address quality concerns and maintain consistent workmanship standards;
- Monitor quality performance through regular site inspections and audits, reporting findings, risks and improvement actions to project management;
- Support continuous improvement by providing quality guidance to site teams and coordinating with third-party inspectors and relevant authorities where required.
What will help you succeed:
- A bachelor’s degree or NVQ Level 4+ qualification in Engineering, Construction Management or a related technical discipline;
- At least 2 years of QA/QC experience in EPC construction projects, ideally within renewable energy, solar PV or other large-scale infrastructure developments;
- Good understanding of construction processes, materials, quality management systems and applicable UK construction standards;
- Practical experience with site inspections, Inspection and Test Plans (ITPs), quality documentation and non-conformance management;
- The ability to interpret technical drawings, specifications and construction documentation to identify potential quality issues;
- A practical, solution-oriented approach to resolving site quality concerns and ensuring corrective actions are completed;
- Confidence in working with engineers, site managers, subcontractors and external inspectors to maintain agreed quality standards;
- Strong organizational skills, attention to technical detail and the ability to manage priorities against construction deadlines;
- Proficiency in Microsoft Office and familiarity with construction project management software;
- A proactive and accountable approach, with the flexibility to respond to changing site and project requirements.
Why you'll enjoy working here:
At SUNOTEC, you'll contribute to the construction of large-scale renewable energy infrastructure across the UK, where the quality of your work has a direct impact on project performance and long-term asset reliability.
You'll work alongside experienced engineering, construction and project management professionals, with the autonomy to identify quality concerns, recommend solutions and influence how work is delivered on site.
Our growing project portfolio will give you exposure to technically demanding EPC construction activities and opportunities to develop your expertise in renewable energy infrastructure.
You'll also benefit from:
- A remuneration package that reflects your experience and the responsibilities of the role;
- The opportunity to contribute to major renewable energy construction projects across the UK;
- Close collaboration with international engineering and construction teams;
- Access to an internal learning platform, structured onboarding and on-the-job training;
- Opportunities to broaden your technical expertise and take on additional responsibilities as our UK operations grow.
Ready to make an impact?
If you're committed to delivering high-quality construction work and want to contribute to the development of large-scale renewable energy infrastructure in the UK, we'd like to hear from you.
Send us your CV in English and join the team building Europe's energy future.
Only shortlisted applicants will be contacted.
Your application and personal data will be treated confidentially and processed in accordance with applicable UK data protection legislation, including the UK General Data Protection Regulation (UK GDPR) and the Data Protection Act 2018.

About us Worley is a global company of energy, chemicals and resources experts headquartered in Australia. We partner with our customers to deliver projects and create value across the life of their assets. We specialize in consulting, engineering, procurement and construction across the project lifecycle, with services extending through to operations and decommissioning. Leveraging extensive experience and AI-enabled delivery, we support customers in navigating complexity as they meet today's needs and transition to more sustainable solutions. Role context -
This vacancy is for a Consultant based in our Bristol or Glasgow offices to support in the delivery and management of contaminated land assessment and remediation projects. This is a full time, permanent (40 hours per week) position and will be part of our Decommissioning, Restoration and Geosciences practice. This position offers excellent career development potential, including training, mentoring and opportunities for international experience. A competitive salary and benefits package will be provided. Core Responsibilities will include the following:
Supporting delivery of contaminated land assessment and remediation projects including desk studies, site investigation, risk assessments, remediation options appraisals, remedial design and verification;
Undertaking the NEC Supervisor role for contaminated land remediation projects and supporting the NEC Project Manager. Training will be provided regarding the Supervisor role, but some previous experience is preferred. Data management: review and interpretation;
Preparation of high-quality technical reports;
Field work including managing contractors on site;
Managing project health and safety on site including preparation of project HSSE plans and method statements; and,
Compliance with Health and Safety policies and procedures
Qualifications -
Knowledge and experience will include the following: Experienced in the delivery of complex site investigation works on industrial facilities in either a lead or supporting capacity;
Demonstrate knowledge of the contaminated land assessment process, human health and environmental risk assessment, development of site conceptual models, soil and groundwater remediation, analytical methodologies and sampling procedures;
Be able to write clear, logical and concise technical reports;
Demonstrate logical and independent thinking;
Strong ability to present, analyse and interpret data to a very high standard.
Possess excellent oral and written communication skills;
Be willing to travel and spend periods of time away on field-based projects across the UK and internationally; and
Be eligible to work in the UK and hold a full valid driving licence.
Qualifications:
Candidates should be educated to degree level (Master’s preferred) in a relevant discipline (e.g. Geology, Applied Environmental Geology, Hydrogeology, Environmental Science, Environmental Consultancy, Geochemistry).
Moving forward together
We want our people to be energized and empowered to drive sustainable impact. So, our focus is on a values-inspired culture that unlocks brilliance through belonging, connection and innovation. We're building a diverse, inclusive and respectful workplace. Creating a space where everyone feels they belong, can be themselves, and are heard.
And we're not just talking about it; we're doing it. We're reskilling our people, leveraging transferable skills, and supporting the transition of our workforce to become experts in today's low carbon energy infrastructure and technology. Whatever your ambition, there's a path for you here.
And there's no barrier to your potential career success. Join us to broaden your horizons, explore diverse opportunities, and be part of delivering sustainable change.
